note('Author page 4; archive 49. This page names antipodal Q points, tangent directions R_i^ω, poles Pε, and meridian directions S_i^ε, and gives their geometric definitions. The graph has 17 boundary/pole/Q vertices plus three central puncture dots, 12 meridian segments, 6 equatorial connecting segments and 12 quarter-circle segments; the labelled quarter-circles carry reciprocal heads. The rear-circle R∞ signs are exchanged relative to C, as required by the visible plus at left and minus at right, not by an assumed orientation convention. Six arc-label superscripts are thick overwritten blots and remain doubtful; the upper-right R0 label has a visible 0, not ∞. The top P’s cancelled ε (crop 050 (515,125,590,205)) and the cancelled rear R∞ label remain provisional. The tangent-line/orientation bijection in (18) can be checked directly: an orientation of a real one-dimensional tangent space selects exactly one of its two positive rays; conversely a positive ray specifies an orientation. The second orientation-set glyph in the lower paragraph is less secure than the ordinary underlined ω used for the three-point cyclic order. The NB writes parenthesized raised ε with an overwritten lower remnant. The large cancelled block has “pour éviter des notations pléthoriques”; C’s “points intérieurs des géodésiques” is not supported. The tiny additional tangent subscript in (19), its cancelled tail, and the last cancelled word are among the weakest readings on this sheet.')
check('050:(18)-oriented-real-line','targeted proof check','In a one-dimensional real tangent space, the two components of its nonzero vectors are the two oriented rays. Choosing one as positive is precisely an orientation; this verifies the local two-element correspondence described after (18).')
hand('overwritten signs and interleaved columns','Scan 050 repeatedly turns superscript signs into solid rectangles; those blots do not justify silently choosing the expected plus/minus pattern. The rear R∞ labels reverse the front-circle left/right sign arrangement. The main-column words orientations de celle-ci are adjacent to, but not part of, the left margin note; H merged the columns. Parenthesized raised ε replaces an overwritten lower mark in the NB.')
